senses.gloss:
मरु॑त् m. pl. (prob. the ‘flashing or shining ones’;
cf. मरीचि and Gk. μαρμαίρω) the storm-gods (Indra's companions and sometimes, e.g. Ragh. xii, 101 = देवाः, the gods or deities in general;
said in the Veda to be the sons of Rudra and Pṛśni q.v., or the children of heaven or of ocean;
and described as armed with golden weapons i.e. lightnings and thunderbolts, as having iron teeth and roaring like lions, as residing in the north, as riding in golden cars drawn by ruddy horses sometimes called Pṛṣatīḥ q.v.;
they are reckoned in Naigh. v, 5 among the gods of the middle sphere, and in RV. viii, 96, 8 are held to be three times sixty in number;
in the later literature they are the children of Diti, either seven or seven times seven in number, and are sometimes said to be led by Mātariśvan), RV. &c. &c.

मर्व् (cf. √ मर्ब्) cl. 1. P. मर्वति, to fill, Dhātup. xv, 69;
to go, move, Vop. :
Caus. मर्वयति, to utter a partic. sound (v.l. for मार्ज्), Dhātup. xxxii, 106.

मार्ग् (properly Nom. fr. मार्ग; cf. √ मृग्) cl. 1. 10. P. (Dhātup. xxxiv, 39) मार्गति, मार्गयति (ep. also Ā. मार्गते; pf. ममार्ग Gr.; aor. अमार्गीत्, ib.; fut., मार्गिता, ib.; मार्गेष्यति, R.; inf. मार्गितुम्, R.; ind.p. मार्गित्वा, ib.),
to seek, look for, MBh.; Hariv.; R.;
to search through, ib.;
to seek after, strive to attain, MBh.; Var.; BhP.;
to endeavour to buy, Kathās.;
to request, ask, beg, solicit anything from any one (with abl. of pers. and acc. of thing, or with two acc.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to ask (a girl) in marriage, Śatr.;
 (cl. 10. P. मार्गयति), to purify, adorn;
to go (?), Dhātup. xxxii, 74.
